            "Naming: every tool is prefixed ga_ then verb-first (list/get/run/create/archive/delete), so the read/write split is readable from the name alone.",
            "Descriptions are the agent's only affordance; each one states what the tool returns and that propertyId falls back to GA4_PROPERTY_ID.",
            "Archive-versus-delete is encoded in the tool name so an agent cannot request an operation GA4 does not support.",
            "Errors are written for a reader who can act: the missing-credential message names the environment variable and what it should point at; the missing-property message names both the argument and the env var.",
            "Guard ergonomics are currently weak — the six write tools mutate live property configuration with no confirmation argument and no dry-run mode. Adding an explicit confirm flag is a known design gap.",
            "Preset report tools trade flexibility for one-call answers; their fixed field sets are documented in the descriptions so an agent knows when to fall back to ga_run_report.",
