        {"kind": "h2", "text": "14.1 Competitive / Market Analysis"},
        {"kind": "para", "text": "Public GA4 MCP servers exist, but they generally cover the Data API only and require the operator to trust third-party code with a Google credential. This server is kept in-house because it also covers Admin API writes, shares the credential pattern with google-search-console-mcp, and can be changed to match HaorGrix workflows without waiting on an upstream maintainer."},
        {"kind": "h2", "text": "14.2 Glossary"},
        {"kind": "table", "header": ["Term", "Definition"], "rows": [
            ["GA4", "Google Analytics 4, the event-based analytics property model that replaced Universal Analytics"],
            ["Data API", "Google Analytics Data API v1 — reporting queries against a GA4 property"],
            ["Admin API", "Google Analytics Admin API v1 — property, stream and measurement configuration"],
            ["Property ID", "Numeric GA4 property identifier; the API path prefixes it with properties/"],
            ["Custom dimension / metric", "A property-scoped field derived from an event parameter or user property; can be archived but never deleted"],
            ["Conversion (key) event", "An event name marked as a business outcome in GA4"],
            ["Data stream", "A web or app source feeding events into a GA4 property"],
            ["Sampling", "GA4 answering a large query from a subset of sessions, producing approximate figures"],
            ["Cardinality limit", "GA4 collapsing excess distinct dimension values into an (other) row"],
            ["Quota token", "The unit GA4 charges Data API requests against, capped per property per hour and per day"],
            ["MCP", "Model Context Protocol — the tool interface between an LLM client and this server"],
            ["stdio transport", "MCP over the process's standard input and output"],
        ]},
